WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.710
Every day, in temples and
homes across the world,

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.820
Buddhists chant the same
few words, three times over.

3
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.120
They are going for refuge.

4
00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.360
A refuge is a shelter.

5
00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.870
An ancient verse says that
people, driven by fear,

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.370
run to many refuges: to mountains,
forests and sacred trees.

7
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.060
So what are Buddhists sheltering
from, and where do they go?

8
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.290
In this mission, you'll unpack
the words of that chant,

9
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.240
and the different meanings
each part can carry.

10
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.320
Then you'll test some modern
refuges, such as money and status,

11
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.250
and ask whether any of them can be safe.

12
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.610
Your mission: find out what
Buddhists shelter from,

13
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.470
and where they go for refuge.
